# SCORM player lock (do not regress)

Anthony (2026-11-03): SuccessFactors did not match laptop preview — vertical tabs still used an Introduction tab with Overview text in the instruction well, and moved/resized images sat at default size overlapping copy.

`npm test` must stay green (`src/lib/scormPlayerBundle.test.ts`, `src/lib/draftMedia.test.ts`).

## Invariants (code, not comments)

- **Deploy rebuilds the player.** `npm run build` runs `build:player` before `vite build`. Publish fetches `/scorm-player/index.html` from that deploy. Do not go back to `vite build` alone.
- **LMS iframe fills the stage.** [`splitScormPlayerBundle`](src/services/scormService.ts) sets `html,body,#root{height:100%}`. Scale-to-fit in the packed player needs a real stage height inside SuccessFactors.
- **Float geometry is in the zip.** [`stampFloatingMediaOnCourse`](src/lib/promoteSlideImages.ts) copies live `x/y/width/height` onto `slide.floatingMedia` before package. Do not pack preview-only `floatingImagesMap` and leave slides at default 240×180.
- **Packed player is the preview layout.** Vertical tabs keep Overview left + Instruction. Do not restore a zomako Introduction-tab canvas as the SCORM path.

## How to change this

Change the helpers and add a failing test first. Re-publish the zip after a player rebuild — an old SuccessFactors package will not pick up `main` by itself.
